The door to the mausoleum closed with a sound, and Subaru found himself meeting the eyes of the dragon carved as a single image on the double doors.

He knew it was probably meant to be the Divine Dragon Volcanica, the one depicted on coins as well. But after hearing the tragic love story surrounding Crusch and Prince Fourier, his feelings towards that "Divine Dragon" were even more complicated than before.

"We encountered the real thing on top of the tower, but seeing it in that empty-headed state, it's hard to find talks of pacts with the kingdom or it being the object of the Divine Dragon Church's faith very convincing..."

"Maybe it perks up when necessary. When it's not, it might just be conserving energy, like Otto when he's not working."

"Even Otto when he's not working is still too conscious to be called empty-headed... Wait, since we're comparing him to the Divine Dragon, maybe the citizens would find that an honor?"

At Beatrice's speculation, Subaru tried simulating it in his head, treating Otto like the Divine Dragon, but Otto when he's not working is too busy being silly from the relief of finishing work, so he couldn't get any useful insight. Otto, go easy on the heavy drinking.

In any case――,

"Ferris, what are you going to do after this?"

"After this?"

"Yes. I mean, you can't go back to Crusch-san's place now... It would be hard to, right? You've probably always lived in the same mansion. Do you have somewhere to go?"

On their way to return the mausoleum key to the cemetery caretaker, Emilia asked this, and Ferris, with troubled eyebrows, scratched his cheek with his finger while hesitating to answer.

From that reaction, Emilia's question had likely hit a nerve with Ferris.

Wilhelm had probably told Subaru and the others about Ferris's whereabouts as a difficult decision made out of concern for his future.

Regardless of the circumstances, Crusch and Ferris had dissolved their master-servant relationship. In that situation, Wilhelm, as Crusch's attendant, couldn't act against his master's wishes. Having someone trustworthy check on Ferris's well-being was the utmost consideration Wilhelm could offer in that moment.

And if they were to respond to Wilhelm's consideration to the fullest――,

"Emilia-tan's saying this: How about coming to our place, at least temporarily?"

"Yes, exactly! What do you think? Of course, I don't mean forever. It would be sad to just part ways like this, and I think sometimes you just need time. It took me about a hundred years to accept that I had frozen everyone in my hometown."

"I think that's a bit too patient, even for you."

"Incidentally, Betty wonders if it took her four hundred years to accept Subaru's love."

"I think that's too pitiful, even for him."

Because of the misleading comments from the long-lived pair, Emilia and Beatrice, Rem started looking at Subaru with somewhat pitying eyes. He'd properly clear up that misunderstanding later, but at least, the offer to Ferris now was sincere.

However, upon hearing this, Ferris placed a hand on his own forehead with a "Haha..."

"I had a feeling someone might say that, but I never thought they actually would. I mean, I am a capable and talented healer, so I understand why you'd want me, but..."

"Mm, it's not like I'm saying this as a joke..."

"Yes, yes, of course, I know Emilia-sama is always serious. I'm happy you'd invite me like this. Really, I am."

"...But, the way you're answering..."

"――That's right. It's a kind offer, but I can't say yes."

Shaking his head slowly, Ferris gave a wry smile and declined Emilia's proposal. Subaru strongly wanted to press him on this attitude, but he also understood why he couldn't agree.

Because――,

"Even if we're apart, I still hold Lady Crusch dear. Even if my decision makes victory in the Royal Selection hopeless, I can't just switch to supporting someone else other than Lady Crusch. I can't be that pragmatic about it."

"I-It's okay if you hate me. I just want to make sure you don't wander off somewhere, that you're okay, that you'll let us know you're alright."

"I won't hate you.――Ah, lie. Actually, I do hate you. I've always, always, always hated Emilia-sama, right from the start."

"Eh! Really?!"

Emilia, who had even offered an uncharacteristic bargaining chip, was shocked. Ferris nodded "Yes" to her, then using the mausoleum key, gestured towards Subaru and the others.

"It's not just Emilia-sama. I hated all the other Royal Selection candidates besides Lady Crusch, and their knights too. I hate Beatrice-chan as well, and even though it's practically our first meeting, I hate Rem-chan. And Subaru-kun, I really hate."

"The way you say that makes it sound like I'm the only one you genuinely hate..."

"What makes you think you're not genuinely hated?"

Hearing that retort, Subaru was silenced, unable to say anything.

"...Really, your feelings won't change?"

Even Emilia, having been told that much, understood the intent behind Ferris's declarations of hate. To refuse Emilia's offer, Ferris had used like and dislike as his reason. And it showed that no matter what was said, no matter how he was treated, his feelings of supporting Crusch wouldn't change.

"Please don't worry so much. I might not continue with the Royal Guard... I'll have to talk to the Captain about that, but there are plenty of places that would want me, like the healing hospital or wherever."

"...You're not going to do anything reckless, are you?"

"Reckless? You mean, like, despairing at the world and ending my life...? Me, the person who hates death more than anything in this world?"

"――. Sorry about that."

The joking tone vanished completely as Ferris stated this clearly, and Subaru apologized.

Even if he had to leave Crusch's side, Ferris wouldn't do anything to compromise his identity as the "Blue" and a healer. Subaru chose to believe that.

"Ah, but! This is frustrating! I can't go say anything to Crusch-san, and if my offer to take Ferris in temporarily is refused, there's nothing I can do...!"

"Didn't Ferris-san just scold you for being arrogant?"

"Oh, yes yes, Rem-chan's right."

"But, Rem..."

"――. Some problems can only be solved by the people directly involved, no matter what."

Even though they could observe the tragedy of this misunderstanding, they had no right to intervene and correct it.

Seeing Subaru venting his frustration, Rem lowered her eyes and sighed softly.

"Just like outsiders can't interfere in your master-servant relationship with Emilia-san, or your contract with Beatrice-chan. You and I..."

"Rem?"

"...What relationship do you and I have? What am I to you?"

"Don't suddenly have a moment of self-reflection! You're, you're important to me!"

"Us too! We, Rem, are very, very important!"

"――. Emilia-san, thank you very much."

"What about me?!"

His very existence brushed aside, Subaru's voice cracked as Rem gracefully ignored him.

While Subaru and the others were having this exchange, Beatrice called out "Hey" to Ferris. Still pinching the hem of Subaru's clothes,

"Betty isn't as worried about your future as Subaru and the others are. But, Betty might owe you a huge debt."

"Beatrice-chan-sama owes me? To the great spirit-sama?"

"You saved Subaru when his gate was nearly destroyed from overexerting himself. Unfortunately, Subaru ignored your advice and broke his gate anyway, but it bought us time, I suppose. Without your power, Betty's contract with Subaru wouldn't exist."

"Well... I might be happier about that than I expected."

"Enjoy the feeling to your heart's content. And Betty is the type who always repays her debts. So, if anything happens to you, Betty will help you anytime."

"Even if Subaru-kun is about to fall off a cliff?"

"Betty would pick up Subaru first and then rush over post-haste."

At Beatrice's answer, hands on her hips and letting out a proud "Hmph," Ferris's eyes widened slightly. Then he covered his mouth with his hand and laughed, "Aha."

The impulse to laugh grew stronger, and soon, tears welled up in the corners of Ferris's eyes.

"Ah, this is embarrassing. Don't make me cry, Beatrice-chan-sama."

"So you really are a crybaby, just as you claimed."

At Beatrice's words, Ferris's smile bloomed even more.

△▼△▼△▼△

"If your feelings change, please come visit us anytime, okay? I'll tell everyone to make sure someone will always be there to welcome you! Promise? Can you keep a promise, Ferris?"

"Stray bullet hit me!"

"That's only fair."

Right up until the very moment of parting, Emilia and the others earnestly extended their invitations to him. He knew full well there was no malice or ulterior motive, and refusing them repeatedly, darkening Emilia's face each time, did stir some guilt, but it couldn't be helped.

"It's not that I have any particular feelings about Emilia-sama and the others, you know."

Even though he himself had relinquished the right, Ferris was still Crusch's knight. For him, even temporarily, to take shelter under the banner of another Royal Selection candidate other than Crusch was unthinkable. If anyone found out, it would reflect poorly on Crusch, and more than anything, he was afraid of what Crusch would think of him.

"...In that regard, His Highness was amazing. Weren't you ever scared?"

At the mausoleum, facing the tombstone and sarcophagus, he had intended to confess his regrets for as long as time allowed. Yet, just a short moment later, fresh regrets he wished he could share would well up again. Moping and fretting, even though he'd switched to male attire, the core of his weak-willed nature remained stubbornly unchanged. He truly, deeply despised himself for it.

If there was one single thing he felt he had judged correctly――,

"I'm glad I was the one to say it."

As he'd told Emilia and the others, suggesting his own dismissal as a knight was his own doing. From the moment he decided to accept the Divine Dragon Church's offer and borrow the power of the Pillar of Filiorg's sacrament, he was prepared to lose the right to be by Crusch's side. But his soul couldn't bear to wait for Crusch to be the one to utter those words. So he said it first, preventing Crusch from having to be the one to cut him loose.――What was this? He'd tried to praise his own correct judgment, but it was just another display of the weak-willed nature he despised.

"I'm nothing but a liar..."

He thought he'd made the right decision. A lie.

He asked if Fourier had been scared. A lie.

He said he had no particular feelings about Emilia and the others. A lie.

Suggesting his own dismissal was to protect his own fragile heart. And he knew that even Fourier had to muster his courage whenever he invited Crusch somewhere.

And he couldn't possibly feel nothing about the rapid advances of Emilia and the others――especially the exploits of Subaru, who shared the same position as a knight――who, despite their overwhelmingly disadvantageous starting point, had achieved numerous feats and greatly troubled the high-ranking nobles due to her half-elf heritage.

In fact, Ferris had never asked Subaru about the state of his right hand, now ungloved.

Since Subaru never brought it up himself, Ferris could imagine it was probably a method difficult to apply to Crusch's treatment. But imagination was just imagination. He didn't seek confirmation. The reason was clear: he was running away from the possibility that there might have been an answer other than relying on the Divine Dragon Church.

Everything, it seemed, was prioritized towards his own escape from pain.

"Do I... truly care about anyone...?"

If he truly cared for someone, shouldn't he have valued their non-negotiable feelings above all? Knowing the prayer Crusch had vowed at Fourier's grave, shouldn't he have sought a path that wouldn't extinguish her wish, even if it meant she continued to suffer from an incurable affliction?

Wasn't it that very anger from confronting an unacceptable reality that reminded Crusch of Fourier and made her, of all people, realize the heartlessness of Ferris's actions?

What if the confusion in Crusch's "memories" triggered by remembering Fourier Lugunica was born from anger at Ferris's actions, which had trampled on that vow? Perhaps Ferris was hated not only by Crusch but also by Fourier.

"――Tch, stop it, this is meaningless."

He realized he was, again, pretending to blame himself while searching for words to comfort himself.

Instead of wasting time on such trivial matters, he needed to establish his future position, to stop worrying Emilia and the others, and Wilhelm, who was now caught between them and Crusch.

The truth was, he had no reason left to continue as a knight. He still held the title of "Blue," so if he approached a healing hospital or magical research institute, he would be more than welcome. Securing employment was easy, but just drifting aimlessly served no purpose.

Using these healing hands to continue saving people was a given, but he had other desires as well.

Even if the right to desire them had been thrown away by Ferris――no, by Felix Argyle himself.

"――Ah, I'm relieved. I was worried we might miss each other."

Suddenly, on his way back from the cemetery, glaring at the cobblestones of the noble district, Ferris's ears twitched, reacting to a voice directed at him.

He stopped and looked forward. Standing in the middle of the road was a single figure――a familiar one.

A man with dull gold hair and deep blue eyes. His tall, slender frame was clad in a well-tailored suit, and his neatly trimmed hair and beard gave him an elegant air. Given the man's profession, this wasn't surprising at all.

After all, he was――,

"――Russell Fellow, was it? You're from the Chamber of Commerce, aren't you?"

"Yes, that's correct. I'm very honored you remember me. For our part, would you prefer to be called Ferris-sama? Or Felix-sama?"

"...Either's fine. Whatever you prefer."

"Then, if I may take you up on that, I'll use Felix-sama. In my line of work, using formal names rather than nicknames tends to avoid various inconveniences."

"Hmm."

Ferris winked one eye at the man who bowed with polite gestures――Russell Fellow.

He was a shrewd operator serving as the representative of the capital's Chamber of Commerce, famous for being exceptionally capable even among the battle-hardened merchants of the royal capital. In fact, during the White Whale subjugation battle, they had relied on him for supplies and transport, so the Crusch camp was not unconnected to him.

"Having said that, I can't really entertain any money-making propositions right now, you know? Unfortunately..."

"Your master-servant contract with Duchess Karsten has been dissolved. Yes, I am aware of that."

"...Your ears are too quick. It's scary."

Having said that, Ferris reflected that he'd been foolish to lead the conversation that way.

Because Russell had clearly been lying in wait for Ferris. Nothing like this had ever happened before. If he was doing something like this today of all days, it could only be because he had a reason to take such action.

And then, one more thing he was foolishly slow to realize.

"...Does this road usually have so few people passing through at this time of day?"

"――――"

Russell stood in the middle of the road, about ten meters from Ferris. Around both Russell and Ferris, no presence approached the streets of the noble district. This would be understandable late at night or early morning, but not at this hour before sunset. And when something impossible happens, there is always a reason.

In this case, the one causing that reason was――,

"Felix-sama, there is something I would very much like to discuss with you. If you wouldn't mind, might I invite you to dinner at my residence? That is, if you haven't yet decided where to go."

"Here to recruit me now that I'm off the leash? Sorry, but that offer is――"

"――No, it's not a recruitment. Actually, this conversation is mandatory."

Slowly, Russell shook his head as if lamenting.――In an instant, a cold blade was pressed against Ferris's slender neck, placed there by someone who had appeared right behind him.

"――Tch!"

Ferris caught his breath, his movements frozen. Taken by surprise, he could do nothing. All he could tell was that the blade was a slender, curved sword with a deep curve, and that the person standing behind him was considerably taller than himself.――No, that and,

"...You don't seem like just a merchant, do you?"

"Who can say? I do wish I were, though."

Russell closed the distance step by step. With a blade at his throat, Ferris, unable to do anything, at least tried not to avert his eyes, and hated himself again for it.

How could he have assumed such a cold-eyed man was an ordinary person?

He bit his lip tightly, suppressing any whimper or groan. This was the utmost he could do now, Ferris admonished himself.

Looking closely at Ferris, Russell's eyes remained cold as he spoke.

"Now that you are no longer the Duchess's knight, I have no hesitation in interrogating you. You will tell me.――About the 'Undying King's Sacrament' passed down in the Argyle family."
